# Opt into npm's audit service, at the endpoint that the image's npm POSTs to at install time.
# - The endpoint is measured on Node 24.19.0 with npm 11.17.0, not guessed. The proxy refuses and
#   logs an older npm's /-/npm/v1/security/audits/quick, which npm treats as non-fatal.
# - npm sends a package/version inventory to the public registry. The inventory may include
#   private-registry and git dependency names.
# - The line also lets any sandbox process send any body to that one path. Every other registry
#   POST and every PUT stays refused.
# - The response supplies install-time warnings and does not fail npm install. Use an explicit
#   `npm audit --audit-level=high` when findings should fail a job.
# - Leaving this line out blocks the automatic inventory disclosure and the POST-body channel, but
#   not the lower-bandwidth channel in allowed GET URLs (SECURITY.md, "Exfiltration through allowed
#   network traffic").
allow https://registry.npmjs.org/-/npm/v1/security/advisories/bulk method=POST
